(7504387, 1196088, 92577, '<td valign="top">Great to see you up there in more ways than one!</td>', 'Great to see you up there in more ways than one!', '2017-03-08 08:19:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504389, 1196102, 118154, '<td valign="top">In my view it is too fuzzy and has no real interest</td>', 'In my view it is too fuzzy and has no real interest', '2017-03-08 08:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504391, 1195954, 12611, '<td valign="top">Nicely sparse and water-droplety. Congrats.</td>', 'Nicely sparse and water-droplety. Congrats.', '2017-03-08 08:48:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504393, 1196196, 121362, '<td valign="top">@tanguera: I think the weather is better in Finland, but where in Finland is a big factor as the aurora circle goes over part of Finlanda and Norway but covers all Iceland.<br/>Planning, follow the aurora forecast, some luck and then simply go out and stay there.  Last week I was out every night for some 4-8 hours, that paid off well.</td>', '@tanguera: I think the weather is better in Finland, but where in Finland is a big factor as the aurora circle goes over part of Finlanda and Norway but covers all Iceland.Planning, follow the aurora forecast, some luck and then simply go out and stay there.  Last week I was out every night for some 4-8 hours, that paid off well.', '2017-03-08 08:53:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504395, 1195802, 54446, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JakeKurdsjuk:</b></div><hr/><i> Your blues got oversaturated during the structuring of the background, OOF areas. Striking bird and the detail there is wonderful, but you need to pull back the details in the areas you don''t want them. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>My sky is quite blue.  I''m sorry you do not live in a place with a blue sky.  In your area, it''s likely air pollution or humidity causing dispersion of light rays.  Maybe you should travel more.</td>', 'Originally posted by JakeKurdsjuk: Your blues got oversaturated during the structuring of the background, OOF areas. Striking bird and the detail there is wonderful, but you need to pull back the details in the areas you don''t want them.  My sky is quite blue.  I''m sorry you do not live in a place with a blue sky.  In your area, it''s likely air pollution or humidity causing dispersion of light rays.  Maybe you should travel more.', '2017-03-08 08:57:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504397, 1195879, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/>Good old Iceland! Another lovely landscape from this wonderful part of the world that has been well composed. I wont labour the point but my main criticisms would be those already expressed about sharpening and saturation. I always fid it quite intriguing just how powerful and dominant a colour red is! The two people to the right and the smaller one a little higher up they really draw the eye, I think there would be a strong argument for some desat at least on the two. Apart from this Chris you have a lovely image that has been well received by your viewers, congrats on making the front page.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge. Good old Iceland! Another lovely landscape from this wonderful part of the world that has been well composed. I wont labour the point but my main criticisms would be those already expressed about sharpening and saturation. I always fid it quite intriguing just how powerful and dominant a colour red is! The two people to the right and the smaller one a little higher up they really draw the eye, I think there would be a strong argument for some desat at least on the two. Apart from this Chris you have a lovely image that has been well received by your viewers, congrats on making the front page.', '2017-03-08 09:09:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504399, 1195875, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/>Weve probably all been there at some point, putting the camera away too early, so pleased you didnt here Drake, well done. A nicely composed shot with the emphasis clearly on that fiery sky, youve caught it all at just the right moment with the sun lighting the bottom of the cloud in a most pleasing way. I like the counter-balance of the lighthouse and your timing to wait for some illumination form it too. I think there is scope to tweak the brightness a little to increase its appeal but still a lovely image Drake.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge. Weve probably all been there at some point, putting the camera away too early, so pleased you didnt here Drake, well done. A nicely composed shot with the emphasis clearly on that fiery sky, youve caught it all at just the right moment with the sun lighting the bottom of the cloud in a most pleasing way. I like the counter-balance of the lighthouse and your timing to wait for some illumination form it too. I think there is scope to tweak the brightness a little to increase its appeal but still a lovely image Drake.', '2017-03-08 09:18:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504403, 1195869, 167587, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> a broad embrace. we can feed at leisure. the cat has finished the night. 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you. I can feel it too!</td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: a broad embrace. we can feed at leisure. the cat has finished the night. 10   Thank you. I can feel it too!', '2017-03-08 09:33:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504404, 1195032, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/>First of all, welcome to DPC Srikanth. I would say youve made a very commendable start to your infant photography, this is very well executed with the all-important eye nice and sharp. There is an air of vulnerability mixed with curiosity that makes this a very appealing image. The DOF is good with nice soft focus in the fore and background. I like that you have chosen to present this in mono which in itself is quite unusual as most shots at this early age are done in colour. I think a little judicious cropping of the right to bring the child more off-centre would improve the end result but all in all a great image, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge. First of all, welcome to DPC Srikanth. I would say youve made a very commendable start to your infant photography, this is very well executed with the all-important eye nice and sharp. There is an air of vulnerability mixed with curiosity that makes this a very appealing image. The DOF is good with nice soft focus in the fore and background. I like that you have chosen to present this in mono which in itself is quite unusual as most shots at this early age are done in colour. I think a little judicious cropping of the right to bring the child more off-centre would improve the end result but all in all a great image, well done.', '2017-03-08 09:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504406, 1196102, 156466, '<td valign="top">My first reaction to seeing this was, "And...?" It''s something I ask myself a lot with macro photography (which yours technically isn''t), my own especially. This is well done for the most part, but outside of that I''m left to wonder why you are showing it to me, which is why I am one of your 5''s.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-03-08 10:04:08.</i></td>', 'My first reaction to seeing this was, "And...?" It''s something I ask myself a lot with macro photography (which yours technically isn''t), my own especially. This is well done for the most part, but outside of that I''m left to wonder why you are showing it to me, which is why I am one of your 5''s.', '2017-03-08 10:02:29.000000', '2017-03-08 10:04:08.000000', 0),
(7504408, 1196196, 58482, '<td valign="top">not fair living in Iceland and all</td>', 'not fair living in Iceland and all', '2017-03-08 10:23:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504409, 1196088, 112739, '<td valign="top">Well done Kees! This has the Kees signature all over it. I bet the stone towers are very impressive to see up close. Congratulations on the Red.</td>', 'Well done Kees! This has the Kees signature all over it. I bet the stone towers are very impressive to see up close. Congratulations on the Red.', '2017-03-08 10:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504410, 1196196, 53094, '<td valign="top">This is an amazing photograph! I don''t have any idea of how to compete with something like this.  Two years ago, your photo would have garnered a vote in at least the mid 7s...I can''t believe it only scored a 6.8.</td>', 'This is an amazing photograph! I don''t have any idea of how to compete with something like this.  Two years ago, your photo would have garnered a vote in at least the mid 7s...I can''t believe it only scored a 6.8.', '2017-03-08 10:26:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504412, 1196052, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/>Well done Ronnie, a cracking image with a cracking lens, a great start with your new acquisition. Your chosen technique of manual focus has undoubtedly saved the day here, so often when there are foreground reeds as here the focus will suddenly flip just at that critical moment, you have avoided that problem, well done. As for the image itself well, it really has everything, down to good timing and patience on your part. You really have got your wildlife shots well nailed. As for the pee, I think I might too in that situation!</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge. Well done Ronnie, a cracking image with a cracking lens, a great start with your new acquisition. Your chosen technique of manual focus has undoubtedly saved the day here, so often when there are foreground reeds as here the focus will suddenly flip just at that critical moment, you have avoided that problem, well done. As for the image itself well, it really has everything, down to good timing and patience on your part. You really have got your wildlife shots well nailed. As for the pee, I think I might too in that situation!', '2017-03-08 10:45:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504414, 1196196, 185793, '<td valign="top">Iceland and Auroras are so in my bucket list. Glad I was able to see and feel from your photo. Stunning capture!</td>', 'Iceland and Auroras are so in my bucket list. Glad I was able to see and feel from your photo. Stunning capture!', '2017-03-08 10:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504415, 1196088, 185793, '<td valign="top">Love the capture of this place and hope to see it in person one day. Great capture and the clouds definitely added drama to this whole scene.</td>', 'Love the capture of this place and hope to see it in person one day. Great capture and the clouds definitely added drama to this whole scene.', '2017-03-08 10:59:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504417, 1195466, 185793, '<td valign="top">I''ve been wanting to visit Yosemite for years. Capturing this horsetail fall fire has been in my bucket list. I''m glad you did it justice!</td>', 'I''ve been wanting to visit Yosemite for years. Capturing this horsetail fall fire has been in my bucket list. I''m glad you did it justice!', '2017-03-08 11:04:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504420, 1196215, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/>What a brightly coloured conspicuous little bird you have captured here. That blue plumage is really quite striking. Its a lovely pose with bird looking into the frame with a nice profile of his beak and features. The twisted silver twigs of the tree to are quite remarkable, I like the way youve composed with the bird on the left with everything flowing to the right. All in all a great shot janine, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a significant contribution to the challenge. What a brightly coloured conspicuous little bird you have captured here. That blue plumage is really quite striking. Its a lovely pose with bird looking into the frame with a nice profile of his beak and features. The twisted silver twigs of the tree to are quite remarkable, I like the way youve composed with the bird on the left with everything flowing to the right. All in all a great shot janine, well done.', '2017-03-08 11:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504423, 1195995, 19825, '<td valign="top">I was taken by this one. Nice shot. I was one of your 8s.</td>', 'I was taken by this one. Nice shot. I was one of your 8s.', '2017-03-08 11:25:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504424, 1196109, 19825, '<td valign="top">Fascinating image. Nicely captured.</td>', 'Fascinating image. Nicely captured.', '2017-03-08 11:26:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504425, 1195529, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/>I think your commenters have given you some useful critique here. They are all correct to a degree, unfortunately this is not quite working because there feels a general underexposure combined with some rim lighting together with stray lighting that is partially illuminating areas that dont really help the end result. I think you are to be commended for trying to create something original probably of a low key nature but it didnt quite work to its best. I do quite like it but what lets it down most is the rim lighting of the leg its counter to the feel of everything else going on here</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a contribution to the challenge. I think your commenters have given you some useful critique here. They are all correct to a degree, unfortunately this is not quite working because there feels a general underexposure combined with some rim lighting together with stray lighting that is partially illuminating areas that dont really help the end result. I think you are to be commended for trying to create something original probably of a low key nature but it didnt quite work to its best. I do quite like it but what lets it down most is the rim lighting of the leg its counter to the feel of everything else going on here', '2017-03-08 11:29:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504427, 1196088, 121362, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the red. This is a great shot.</td>', 'Congrats on the red. This is a great shot.', '2017-03-08 11:36:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504428, 1194750, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/> A gruesome but interesting fish skeleton. I like the diagonal that youve used for your composition and the lighting is picking out the detail and texture which works well against the pebbly background. The colours are good too. I dont really get the feeling suggested by the title, it is what it is a skeletal fish head, a good documentary photograph but not really anything more than that, sorry Erin.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a contribution to the challenge.  A gruesome but interesting fish skeleton. I like the diagonal that youve used for your composition and the lighting is picking out the detail and texture which works well against the pebbly background. The colours are good too. I dont really get the feeling suggested by the title, it is what it is a skeletal fish head, a good documentary photograph but not really anything more than that, sorry Erin.', '2017-03-08 11:36:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504432, 1195954, 121362, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon, Nice work.</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon, Nice work.', '2017-03-08 11:38:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504433, 1196149, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that makes a contribution to the challenge.<br/> <br/> First of all welcome to DPC Jeannie. You have a colourful and well executed cityscape with good detail throughout. Your chosen aperture has given you a good DOF and long exposure to create some unique motion in the clouds above the buildings. I like the contrasts between the dark blue of the sky and green/yellow of the base. A minor improvement, I think would be to crop the pole on the extreme left and the lamp on the extreme right, they are just a little close to the edge and the scene behind it would probably benefit a little too.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that makes a contribution to the challenge.  First of all welcome to DPC Jeannie. You have a colourful and well executed cityscape with good detail throughout. Your chosen aperture has given you a good DOF and long exposure to create some unique motion in the clouds above the buildings. I like the contrasts between the dark blue of the sky and green/yellow of the base. A minor improvement, I think would be to crop the pole on the extreme left and the lamp on the extreme right, they are just a little close to the edge and the scene behind it would probably benefit a little too.', '2017-03-08 11:42:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504435, 1196124, 30049, '<td valign="top">57th?!  Dang.  I thought it was a very fun, and well titled, photo.  :-)  Maybe with a square crop this would have done better?  FWIW, I gave it an 8.</td>', '57th?!  Dang.  I thought it was a very fun, and well titled, photo.  :-)  Maybe with a square crop this would have done better?  FWIW, I gave it an 8.', '2017-03-08 11:53:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504448, 1196196, 92577, '<td valign="top">love it!</td>', 'love it!', '2017-03-08 13:22:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504465, 1195466, 19825, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot. Nicely done.</td>', 'Lovely shot. Nicely done.', '2017-03-08 14:55:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504466, 1196227, 30214, '<td valign="top">wow, isn''t that amazing! truly small world. BTW, your vantage point is better than mine... a helicopter? (btw, sent you a PM)<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lei_73:</b></div><hr/><i> Aloha, dear Lev!<br/>I could not stop laughing for few minutes! Ok, may be not really laughing, but certainly be amazed by the fact how our world is so tiny!<br/>This could have been my submission for free study if I had not lost track of time...<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1196488" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/170000-174999/170018/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1196488.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/170000-174999/170018/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1196488.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/170000-174999/170018/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1196488.jpg"/></a> <br/>And I even saw you! I forgot where exactly, probably some market, but I told my husband that there''s a person who looks exactly like Lev Tsimring! Too bad you''ve disappeared too quickly...<br/>Life is funny! :-) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'wow, isn''t that amazing! truly small world. BTW, your vantage point is better than mine... a helicopter? (btw, sent you a PM)Originally posted by lei_73: Aloha, dear Lev!I could not stop laughing for few minutes! Ok, may be not really laughing, but certainly be amazed by the fact how our world is so tiny!This could have been my submission for free study if I had not lost track of time... And I even saw you! I forgot where exactly, probably some market, but I told my husband that there''s a person who looks exactly like Lev Tsimring! Too bad you''ve disappeared too quickly...Life is funny! :-) ', '2017-03-08 15:03:35.000000', NULL, 0),
