(7504859, 1196196, 121362, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by srdanz:</b></div><hr/><i> Love it! When I was in Iceland, they told me to under no circumstances stop my car in the middle of the road and observe the nature :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, as they say in the TV shows: This stunt was performed by trained professionals ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by srdanz: Love it! When I was in Iceland, they told me to under no circumstances stop my car in the middle of the road and observe the nature :)   Well, as they say in the TV shows: This stunt was performed by trained professionals ;)', '2017-03-10 19:14:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7504909, 1195466, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Zeus:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you, Jomari.<br/>But what''s a HM? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>HM = Honorable Mention -- the star you get for 4th or 5th place.<br/> <br/>When I was a kid I was in Yosemite when they had an actual "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yosemite_Firefall" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Firefall</a> from Glacier Point, but I didn''t know about this phenomenon -- great shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by Zeus: Thank you, Jomari.But what''s a HM?  HM = Honorable Mention -- the star you get for 4th or 5th place. When I was a kid I was in Yosemite when they had an actual "Firefall from Glacier Point, but I didn''t know about this phenomenon -- great shot.', '2017-03-11 15:01:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7505143, 1195802, 182284, '<td valign="top">I hear owls very close to my house, how did you find this beautiful creature. I don''t know if he or she travels further south for the winter but I''ve heard it very close to my house. I saw one in a tree next to my house a couple of years ago but not since then. I think it was a Barred owl. What is the one in your photo? Oh and BTW our sky''s are very blue here in the Ouachita Mountain range. I love the blue sky''s.<br/>Very nice shot, I''m jealous. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-03-13 15:56:24.</i></td>', 'I hear owls very close to my house, how did you find this beautiful creature. I don''t know if he or she travels further south for the winter but I''ve heard it very close to my house. I saw one in a tree next to my house a couple of years ago but not since then. I think it was a Barred owl. What is the one in your photo? Oh and BTW our sky''s are very blue here in the Ouachita Mountain range. I love the blue sky''s.Very nice shot, I''m jealous. :)', '2017-03-13 15:50:04.000000', '2017-03-13 15:56:24.000000', 0),
(7527710, 1195936, 185773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jgirl57:</b></div><hr/><i> That is what I am talking about. My favorite nice work </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi jgirl157, My apology it took so long to reply you, I truly appreciate your comment an totally delighted that I have at least one photographer that understand what I shoot. I feel so alone sending in macro shoot everytime and must let you know I am really glad for your support. Thank you very much.<br/> <br/>Sincerely your''s,<br/> <br/>Roger New<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by jgirl57: That is what I am talking about. My favorite nice work   Hi jgirl157, My apology it took so long to reply you, I truly appreciate your comment an totally delighted that I have at least one photographer that understand what I shoot. I feel so alone sending in macro shoot everytime and must let you know I am really glad for your support. Thank you very much. Sincerely your''s, Roger New', '2017-08-08 07:27:17.000000', NULL, 0);
